# Do the pairwise maps between goals form one consistent system?

Generated by `equiv3.py` (exploratory). The 12 linear maps M(A→B) of `equiv2.py` (ridge on differences at the input of block 2, 12288 training pairs each), composed and inverted, evaluated on 4096 random same-step pairs of test decisions (posteriors ≥ 0.5 apart) and, for the effect of a composition, on `equiv.py`'s A-equivalent, C-different test pairs (451 (424–587) per triple). Means over the 24 ordered triples / 12 ordered pairs, medians (min–max) over six models.

## Composition: M(B→C) M(A→B) Δ_A against M(A→C) Δ_A

| prediction of Δ_C from Δ_A | held-out R² for Δ_C | cosine with Δ_C | R² against the direct map's prediction | cosine with it | norm / direct's |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| direct map M(A→C) | 0.95 (0.94–0.96) | 0.95 (0.95–0.96) | 1 | 1 | 1 |
| **composed M(B→C) M(A→B)** | **0.94 (0.93–0.95)** | 0.95 (0.94–0.95) | **0.99 (0.98–0.99)** | 0.99 (0.98–0.99) | 0.98 (0.98–0.98) |
| untransformed Δ_A | 0.36 (0.24–0.42) | | | | |

Over all 144 (model, triple) cases the composed prediction's R² against the direct map's ranges 0.97–0.99 (lowest decile 0.98).

**Effect under C** on the A-equivalent, C-different pairs (the vector added to x1 under C; share of pairs whose C-decisions differ that switch to b2's):

| vector added under C | C's decision to b2's |
|---|---|
| direct C-written difference Δ_C | 0.91 (0.89–0.96) |
| direct map M(A→C) Δ_A | 0.86 (0.80–0.89) |
| **composed M(B→C) M(A→B) Δ_A** | **0.85 (0.79–0.89)** |
| untransformed Δ_A | 0.33 (0.24–0.40) |
| random, Δ_C's norm | 0.04 (0.02–0.06) |

Composed minus direct map, per (model, triple): mean -0.014, range -0.13 to +0.08.

